dpdk: mlx4 RX queue interrupts, consumed through the PMD

net_mlx4 shared a driver entry with qede and bnxt that left
enable_rxq_int unset, so VPP never probed for interrupts and gave the
queues no event file; setting rx-mode adaptive or interrupt on a
ConnectX-3 port failed with VNET_API_ERROR_UNIMPLEMENTED (-9). The mlx4
PMD supports RX interrupts, so give it its own entry with enable_rxq_int.

That alone is not enough. mlx4's queue fd is an ibverbs completion
channel, not an eventfd: an event must be taken with ibv_get_cq_event and
acked, which the PMD does in rx_intr_disable. VPP read 8 bytes from the
fd, which fails on a completion channel (an event is 16 bytes), so the
event was never consumed, the CQ arm sequence never advanced and the
queue raised no further interrupts: in adaptive mode on a ConnectX-3
every packet was lost once the workers slept. Switching back to polling
also failed, because rx_intr_disable returns -EAGAIN when no event is
pending.

A new driver flag, int_ack_by_disable (set for net_mlx4), makes
dpdk_rx_read_ready consume pending events with rte_eth_dev_rx_intr_disable
instead of read(), and the switch to polling treats -EAGAIN from it as
success. dpdk_port_conf_t keeps its size (a spare bit of the u16 field).

Tested on a ConnectX-3 (i5-9300H, 2 workers, 2 RX queues, NAT44-EI, 64 B):
idle workers at 0.9% CPU instead of 100%, no loss from 1 kpps to 1 Mpps
while workers wake from interrupts, 7.3-8.1 Mpps above the NIC ceiling as
when polling, and polling/adaptive switches work both ways.

--- a/src/plugins/dpdk/device/common.c
+++ b/src/plugins/dpdk/device/common.c
@@ -362,8 +362,20 @@
   vnet_hw_if_rx_queue_t *rxq = vnet_hw_if_get_rx_queue (vnm, qidx);
   dpdk_device_t *xd = vec_elt_at_index (dm->devices, rxq->dev_instance);
 
-  u64 b;
-  CLIB_UNUSED (ssize_t size) = read (uf->file_descriptor, &b, sizeof (b));
+  if (xd->conf.int_ack_by_disable)
+    {
+      /* Take every pending completion event off the channel and ack it;
+	 the PMD returns -EAGAIN once none is left. Without this the CQ is
+	 never re-armed and the queue raises no further interrupts. */
+      for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++)
+	if (rte_eth_dev_rx_intr_disable (xd->port_id, rxq->queue_id))
+	  break;
+    }
+  else
+    {
+      u64 b;
+      CLIB_UNUSED (ssize_t size) = read (uf->file_descriptor, &b, sizeof (b));
+    }
   if (qidx < vec_len (dpdk_rxq_int_armed))
     dpdk_rxq_int_armed[qidx] = 0;
   if (rxq->mode != VNET_HW_IF_RX_MODE_POLLING)
--- a/src/plugins/dpdk/device/device.c
+++ b/src/plugins/dpdk/device/device.c
@@ -740,7 +740,12 @@
     return clib_error_return (0, "unsupported op (is the interface up?)", rv);
   if (mode == VNET_HW_IF_RX_MODE_POLLING &&
       !(xd->flags & DPDK_DEVICE_FLAG_INT_UNMASKABLE))
-    rv = rte_eth_dev_rx_intr_disable (xd->port_id, qid);
+    {
+      rv = rte_eth_dev_rx_intr_disable (xd->port_id, qid);
+      /* -EAGAIN: no completion event was pending, nothing to consume */
+      if (rv == -EAGAIN && xd->conf.int_ack_by_disable)
+	rv = 0;
+    }
   else if (mode == VNET_HW_IF_RX_MODE_POLLING)
     {
       rxq = vec_elt_at_index (xd->rx_queues, qid);
--- a/src/plugins/dpdk/device/dpdk.h
+++ b/src/plugins/dpdk/device/dpdk.h
@@ -126,6 +126,9 @@
